{"skill":{"slug":"context7","displayName":"Context7 MCP"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1769015493568,"changelog":"Added best practices section for search, context, versioning, and quality filtering","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"package-lock.json","size":58312,"sha256":"3dd695f6e457c50469d601dcff4e999c6c28f4ceaf71ffb8d8fde4b4a57c05b7","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":425,"sha256":"754c5054f445994dd458971b2958fda4537788bd4c53f70893522930e00a9984","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"query.ts","size":4761,"sha256":"251f259b0a0a313346343088a09bedc39bfbc113c1fdd70e05dd384e1bedb3aa","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"skill.md","size":4679,"sha256":"cd080f919e8d2aa0ac46c82d8e24640b2dd084046a03f42ffd828d3aa398577a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tsconfig.json","size":286,"sha256":"db4c87695c682d8ce97a55367360f04bdc2830e02d1bc2cb1365d8507b8522c4","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2328,"sha256":"13fc8d2763755365cec659cc72fd751e2719974bb6dd872d6992b091dc1dc989","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015630745,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0658bdb2b383609a3257567341caa1b533ad994c7075f48f7727d32dc9f43e87","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0658bdb2b383609a3257567341caa1b533ad994c7075f48f7727d32dc9f43e87","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: context7\nVersion: 1.0.3\n\nThe skill is designed to query the Context7 API for documentation, which aligns with its stated purpose. The `query.ts` script reads an API key from environment variables or a local `.env` file and uses it to authenticate requests to `https://context7.com` endpoints. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized destinations, malicious code execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts in `SKILL.md`. While the `package-lock.json` reveals dependencies like `cross-spawn` and web server frameworks (`express`, `hono`) within the `mcp-client` SDK, these are not directly utilized in a harmful way by the provided `query.ts` script, nor are there instructions for the agent to misuse them. The overall behavior is consistent with a legitimate API client.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159733366},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":21,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789015630745},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed Context7 documentation-query CLI, with ordinary API-key and network use plus some dependency hygiene issues.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Node, npm, outbound Context7 API access, and a Context7 API key are proportionate to the documented CLI purpose; no broad local file access is present beyond reading the local .env for that key.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The install path asks users to run npm install and the package includes a lockfile, but package.json uses caret ranges, includes apparently unused dependencies, and has scripts for absent read.ts and explore.ts files.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime behavior is user-directed: commands take a library and query, read CONTEXT7_API_KEY from the environment or local .env, and send requests to context7.com. The network/API-key use is disclosed in skill.md, though not expressed as a formal permission block.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No evidence of background workers, scheduled tasks, privilege escalation, tool hijacking, destructive actions, or cross-session persistence beyond an optional user-created .env credential file.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Context7 documentation search/context retrieval, and query.ts implements search and context commands against documented Context7 REST endpoints.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, prefer deterministic installs from the included lockfile, review or remove unused dependencies, and keep the Context7 API key scoped to this service. Expect your library names and search queries to be sent to Context7 when you run the commands.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The scanner's environment/network concern is supported by the code, but the artifact discloses the Context7 API key and exact Context7 endpoints; I treat this as a disclosure note, not hidden access.\n[SC1] unexpected: The unpinned caret dependency ranges are real dependency-hygiene issues; they are not evidence of active malicious behavior, especially with a package-lock.json present.\n[T08] unexpected: The static scan's concern about unnecessary dependencies and install scripts is supported: mcp-client and zod are not imported by query.ts, while npm install can install transitive packages with install scripts. This is a low supply-chain hardening issue, not a purpose mismatch in the skill's runtime behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015630745}}}}}